From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:11:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Name the effect that is not drawn for want of a
 transform graph.

The FIXME gave only a pointer; with the effect's CLSID it says which
built-in effect is still missing, here ColorMatrix for PowerPoint's
recoloured pictures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit bb104cd318fd3517b9acdb16e83450fe25b72ca3)

diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c b/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c
index 9be0b19d471..6e15b0a732e 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c
@@ -640,7 +640,11 @@ static HRESULT d2d_effect_renderer_effect_bounds(struct d2d_effect_renderer *ren
     }
     else
     {
-        FIXME("Effect %p has no transform graph, it is not drawn.\n", effect);
+        CLSID clsid = {0};
+
+        ID2D1Effect_GetValue(&effect->ID2D1Effect_iface, D2D1_PROPERTY_CLSID, D2D1_PROPERTY_TYPE_CLSID,
+                (BYTE *)&clsid, sizeof(clsid));
+        FIXME("Effect %p %s has no transform graph, it is not drawn.\n", effect, debugstr_guid(&clsid));
         hr = E_NOTIMPL;
     }
     --renderer->depth;
